    {
      "version": "1.0.1",
      "channel": "stable",
      "date": "2026-04-19",
      "status": "available",
      "source": {
        "repository": "https://github.com/DreamWeave-MP/Openmw_Config",
        "tag": "1.0.1",
        "revision": "0927f5b6b3611cc179024c3ee1c16e49c0627666"
      },
      "notes": {
        "summary": "First stable release: parsing that matches OpenMW's, Lua bindings, and Flatpak paths.",
        "highlights": "openmw-config 1.0 reads a config chain the way OpenMW does: `config=` entries level by level,\n`replace=` applied as it is read, and line numbers in every parse error. It adds embedded Lua\nbindings with a camelCase API and resolves tokens correctly inside Flatpak.\n",
        "added": [
          "Lua bindings through `mlua`, behind the `lua` feature: `create_lua_module` and a camelCase API.",
          "Flatpak-aware `?userconfig?` and `?userdata?`, and `OPENMW_FLATPAK_ID`.",
          "`default_local_path` and `default_global_path`, for `?local?` and `?global?`, with fallible `try_` variants.",
          "`user_config_ref`, which leaves the configuration in place, and `&str` views of setting values.",
          "`config_chain`, the parser-order record of loaded and skipped configs.",
          "Parse errors carry the line they came from."
        ],
        "changed": [
          "Relicensed under GPL-3.0-or-later.",
          "`dirs` and `shellexpand` are replaced by the standard library. On Windows, the Documents folder comes from the Known Folder API.",
          "Queries on content files, archives, data directories and game settings are indexed."
        ],
        "fixed": [
          "`config=` entries load level by level, siblings before their children, as OpenMW loads them.",
          "`replace=config` discards earlier settings and queued `config=` entries.",
          "`fallback=` values keep their exact spelling through a round trip.",
          "Game settings are deduplicated by key.",
          "Path comparisons normalize separators."
        ],
        "breaking": [
          "Methods that built a `Vec` are gone; collect the iterators instead."
        ]
      },
